# The next DFlash2 block pass starts at a decode round's end: MultiDecoder._prelaunch -> MultiDrafter.prelaunch
# launches the block pass of the streams that will ask for drafts next round, so it runs while rank 0 finishes the
# round (emit, the next plan, the message all-gather) instead of after it. The next round's candidates() only waits
# for it when its streams and pending tokens match and none of their contexts changed since (DraftContext.context_end
# bumps that context's generation; another slot's prompt chunk or admission leaves it valid); else it runs its own
# pass. The same inputs give the same candidates: the same drafts and replies. The decision reads only state every
# rank holds (the round's streams, tokens and depths from the gathered samples, context ends), never Stream.done,
# which rank 0's emit sets alone, so every rank launches the same collectives. Patch 0092's check-and-retry loop is
# kept: the first copy of the candidates goes out with the pass, the retry copies again. TF_GLM_DRAFT_PRELAUNCH=0
# turns it off (checked equal on every rank at startup). tools/draft_prelaunch_check.py.

