+        will ask for drafts next round if nothing changes (``MultiDrafter.prelaunch``), so it runs while rank 0
+        finishes the round and sends the next message instead of after. Only state every rank holds decides it -
+        not ``Stream.done``, which rank 0's emit sets alone (a stop string, a cancelled client) - so every rank
+        launches the same pass and its all-gather pairs up. A next round that differs (a stream left, joined or
+        paused, a short round, copied drafts) runs its own pass; the drafts are the same either way."""
